{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And in the latter end of their kingdom</b> — over Israel." "<b>When the transgressors have reached their fullness</b> — and the meaning is that because the transgressors of Israel were many, therefore they were delivered into the hand of the Greeks." "<b>A king of fierce countenance</b> — he was Antiochus, and his prince was Glinus. And there are some of the Geonim who say that the king of fierce countenance is the Kedarite who arose in the year four thousand and two hundred and fifty-four, and the prophet speaks of one of the four kings who ruled under Alexander, and so he interpreted further in the fourth prophecy, \"And a mighty king shall stand up,\" who is Alexander, and he said: \"And when he stands up, his kingdom shall be broken and split toward the four winds of heaven\" — and behold, this is not as he spoke."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {2 "The number שנ\"ד (254) is read against the context of 'four thousand'; taken literally it yields 4254, which may be corrupt or an abbreviated/defective notation. Resolved by translating the numeral as given."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:32.792975681Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}